I ordered two boxes of pizza from a group called Slice and Dice. The thing that surprised me the most though, is that when I opened the boxes, clowns jumped out and started throwing knives at me with the words Slice and Dice written in blood all over their knives. I'm rather surprised I made it out alive, seeing as how there were over a hundred of those knives flying around my apartment. I guess you can say karma works in miraculous ways, since I did fall for the scam. The clowns did apologize though, and after I looked around I discovered they weren't real knives or blood. They were pieces of pizza crust molded into the shape of knives, and the blood was actually pizza sauce. In the end my pizza was politely handed to me by the clowns and they were on their merry way.
---
In a shocking finding, scientist discovered a herd of unicorns living in a remote, previously unexplored valley, in the Andes Mountains. Even more surprising to the researchers was the fact that the unicorns spoke perfect English.
The researchers, of the Universidad Metropolitana del Sur, were shocked by the fact that they found unicorn tongues written on the walls and walls of the mountain valley and that the language was written in a similar syntax to that of other unicorn languages. The researchers also discovered that they have never before seen such a widespread linguistic communication between humans and an unusual and unusual species. The unicorn tongues could reveal that we are not the only ones that speak these languages.

